<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef generally lower on light to moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice chuck, round and loin cuts generally lower, while the rib cuts weak.  Beef trimmings weak on light to moderate demand and offerings.  - USDA</p>
<p>-------</p>
<p>240 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 68 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>18 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     105.94	105.23	 99.85	 98.83</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.06	 -0.80	  0.01	 -0.63</p>
<p>Rib	  160.59	158.95	151.77	150.31</p>
<p>Chuck	 72.85	 70.64	 73.81	 70.73</p>
<p>Round	 89.64	 89.64	 86.33	 86.33</p>
<p>Loin	 174.78	175.38	153.10	153.38</p>
<p>Brisket     57.63	 57.63	 55.69	 55.69</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  64.69	 64.61	 64.92	 64.76</p>
<p>Flank	 58.03	 58.03	 58.18	 58.18</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
